course: dictionary
lesson: 4504
title: Words from farm life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Haymaking is a noun, a name for a job or activity. «Haymaking is cutting grass, drying it in the sun, turning it and baling it for winter.» The sentence lists the steps in order, so the word names the whole job from start to finish.
explain: The sentence also gives clues about why the job matters. «Wet hay goes mouldy» tells you hay must stay dry, and «damp hay packed in a barn can get hot and even catch fire» shows that the drying must be done carefully.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. In sport, a haymaker is a big wild punch, and haymaking can mean throwing such punches. Context tells you which meaning is right: a story about fields and barns means farm work, while a story about a boxing match means punches.
fact: Haymaking means cutting grass, drying it and gathering it as hay to feed animals in winter.
fact: «Wet hay goes mouldy», so farmers need sunny, dry weather to make good hay.
fact: Make hay while the sun shines means use a good chance while it lasts.
fact: In sport, a haymaker is a big wild punch, and haymaking can mean throwing such punches.
fact: Context clues, such as the other words in the sentence, show you which meaning of a word fits.
exercise: «Haymaking is cutting grass, drying it in the sun, turning it and baling it for winter.» Which step comes first in haymaking? | Baling the hay | *Cutting the grass | Feeding the animals in the barn | Turning the hay over in the field
exercise: What is haymaking? | Selling food at a market | A big wild punch in a boxing match | *Cutting grass, drying it and storing it as hay for animals in winter | Planting seeds in the spring
exercise: «Wet hay goes mouldy.» Why must farmers dry hay well? | So the hay turns into a sweet | So the hay grows taller | *So the hay does not go mouldy | So the hay can float on the river
test: In a boxing story, the text says, «He landed a haymaker in the third round.» What does haymaker mean here? | A farm worker who cuts grass | *A big wild punch | A sunny day in the field | A kind of cart for hay
test: What does the saying «make hay while the sun shines» mean? | *Use a good chance while it lasts | Dry your clothes in a barn | Cut grass only at night | Go to bed early on sunny days
exam: In the sentence «The whole village was busy with haymaking all summer», what does haymaking mean? | A holiday at the seaside | A big wild punch | Painting pictures of the fields | *Cutting, drying and gathering grass as hay for winter
